==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[foreswear]]

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|forsweren||lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|forswerian||to swear falsely|lang=ang}}. More at {{prefix|for|swear|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
*: {{rhymes|ɛə(r)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|forswears|forswearing|forswore|forsworn}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[renounce]] or [[deny]] [[something]], especially under [[oath]].
#* Shakespeare
#*: I {{...}} do '''forswear''' her.
#* Dryden
#*: Like innocence, and as serenely bold / As truth, how loudly he '''forswears''' thy gold!
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To [[commit]] [[perjury]]. 

